<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kurukshetra</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kurukshetra is a city and district in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haryana">Haryana</a>, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a>. In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> tradition it is the battlefield of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahabharata">Mahabharata</a> war and the place where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishna">Krishna</a> taught the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhagavad-gita">Bhagavad Gita</a>, and its sacred tanks, such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahma">Brahma</a> Sarovar, draw pilgrims. The town of Thanesar, capital of the 7th-century king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harsha">Harsha</a>, lies within it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kurukshetra.jpg" alt="Kurukshetra" width="320" height="223" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sid Sharma5911 · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kurukshetra_junction_kkde.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>At Bhagwanpura in the <b>Kurukshetra</b> district of Haryana, large houses may have been the homes of an elite.</blockquote><a href="/culture/painted-grey-ware-culture">Painted Grey Ware culture · Society</a></li><li><blockquote>A much older chronology comes from post-Vedic Hindu texts such as the Mahabharata, the Ramayana and the Puranas, in which the Vedas were received by the seven rishis thousands of years ago and the <b>Kurukshetra</b> War is dated to about 3100 BCE.</blockquote><a href="/culture/vedic-civilisation">Vedic civilisation · Origins</a></li><li><blockquote>The historicity of the <b>Kurukshetra</b> War is unclear; many historians date it to the 10th century BCE, and F. E. Pargiter's reckoning from Puranic genealogies gives about 950 BCE.</blockquote><a href="/work/mahabharata">Mahabharata · Origins</a></li><li><blockquote>The British confiscated Ladwa in 1846, and its lands became part of a British district, now in <b>Kurukshetra</b> district of Haryana.</blockquote><a href="/state/ladwa-state">Ladwa State</a></li><li><blockquote>After the Sikhs captured Sirhind in 1763–64, Sikh sardars divided the surrounding country, and a Sikh family established itself at Thanesar, the old town beside the sacred tanks of <b>Kurukshetra</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/thanesar-state">Thanesar State</a></li></ul></section>
